# rule 24: whether a file is the one the editor saw earlier is judged in
# we_seen.c, by wpe_seen_judge, never by an inode number kept from an earlier
# moment (a file system gives a number back after its file is gone).
# Clause a (r24a) is st_ino and st_dev, b (r24b) a member of a WpeSeen read
# outside we_seen.c, c (r24c) statx and the birth-time names, d (r24d) the
# folder numbers kept by hand and the three-argument identity question, e
# (r24e) a test that asserts "another inode" with nothing held, f (r24f) the
# file the user was shown passed to the mode owner as anything but a WpeSeen
# called shown, g (r24g) a call of the removed bridge wpe_seen_into_stat, kept
# so that it cannot come back.  Each pass deletes the rows of the sites it
# moves onto the owner: N2 the write owner and the assistant's look, N3 the
# mode owner (done: no row of clause f or g is left; the type of the shown
# record is also checked by the compiler, WPE_SHOWN_RECORD in we_write.h), N4
# the assistant's checkpoint and window lookup, N5 the two-look sites and the
# tests.
# N4 (done): the assistant's checkpoint holds its workspace folder open, its
# mode record judges the look at the name against the descriptor's, and its
# remembered Yes is a WpeSeen: no row is left for we_ai_ws.c or we_ai_ui.c.
# N5: the two-look sites and the tests
we_write.c|r24a:write_backup_source|4|N5|site 13: the backup reads the file the write holds
we_write.c|r24a:write_bak_is_ours|4|N5|site 14: the .bak is the one the backup made
we_write.c|r24a:write_restore_by_rename_ok|4|N5|site 15: the name is the file the write used
we_fileop.c|r24a:fileop_job_judge_dst|4|N5|site 17: source and destination are one file
we_fileop.c|r24a:fileop_job_names_target_of_source|4|N5|site 17: source and destination are one file
we_opt.c|r24a:e_opt_same_file|4|N5|site 18: two option files are one
we_prog.c|r24a:e_prj_same_file|4|N5|site 19: two project paths are one
we_startplan.c|r24a:startplan_add_program_startup|4|N5|site 21: a file is the one in HOME
we_startplan.c|r24a:startplan_same_file_as_in|4|N5|site 21: a file is the one in HOME
we_child.c|r24a:wpe_child_tty_name_is|4|N5|site 22: the name is the terminal on the descriptor
test_write_owner.c|r24e:test_an_old_copy_of_ours_is_replaced_by_a_new_inode|1|N5|C-03: "a new inode" asserted by number
test_testdir.c|r24e:test_put_mode_makes_a_new_file_with_its_mode|1|N5|the file is held by a second name made before
# rule 25: the editor's own places and the names it chooses.  r25a lists each
# by-name text face outside the owner with how the user named the path; r25i
# lists the uses of the home folder that are not a place of the editor's own.
# r25b, r25c, r25d, r25e, r25f, r25g and r25h have no line: they are never
# allowed.  The start command's store keeps its own resolver call
# (startcmd_state_dir) because its unit tests link no write owner.
we_ai_ui.c|r25a:ai_transcript_write|1|keep|the transcript name the user typed
we_opt.c|r25a:e_opt_lines_store|1|keep|the options file the options came from; NOFOLLOW for the start folder's xwperc
we_opt.c|r25a:e_save_opt|1|keep|the options file the options came from; NOFOLLOW for the start folder's xwperc
we_prog.c|r25a:e_write_default_prj|1|keep|the project name the user typed in New Project
we_prog.c|r25a:e_wrt_prj_fl|1|keep|the open project's file; NOFOLLOW when a start folder named it
# r25i: getenv("HOME") and getpwuid( outside we_places.c.  The home of a place
# the editor keeps its own files in is asked of wpe_user_home; these are not
# such places.
we_fl_unix.c|r25i:fm_stand_at_home|1|keep|a chdir to the home folder when the working folder or the folder asked for cannot be entered; nothing is written there
we_write.c|r25i:write_user_words|1|keep|getpwuid of the owner's uid, for the name in a sentence; not a home

